# Docker reads only the .dockerignore at the build context root, and both compose
# services build with `context: .` — so this file governs the backend and the
# frontend image alike. Per-app .dockerignore files are never consulted.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist

# Build/run artefacts that have no business in an image. .elasticbeanstalk/logs
# alone was 367MB of the backend context.
**/.elasticbeanstalk
**/logs
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.turbo
**/.DS_Store
**/.git

# Secrets stay out of images by default. Frontend .env is an exception: Next
# inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_* at build time, and the Dockerfile deletes the file (and
# any copy under standalone/) before the runtime stage. Backend .env stays out.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.*.example
!apps/frontend/.env

